e","target":"https://www.spokesman.com/stories/2024/feb/28/idaho-senate-passes-bill-to-let-therapists-refuse-/?utm_source=chatgpt.com","line":50}],"metadata":{"title":"Would Idahoans send an independent to the Senate? Todd Achilles kicks off campaign in North Idaho to find out","source":"https://www.spokesman.com/stories/2025/aug/12/would-idahoans-send-an-independent-to-the-senate-t/","author":["[[Orion Donovan Smith]]"],"published":"2025-08-12","created":"2026-07-24","description":"LEWISTON – It’s been more than half a century since Idaho voters sent anyone other than a Republican to the U.S. Senate. Now, a former Democratic state lawmaker is launching an independent bid to unseat an incumbent GOP senator in 2026, hoping that Idahoans share his frustration with both parties.","tags":["#idaho"]},"task_lines":[],"tasks":{},"codeblock_ranges":[]},